A domain is a module with use Taskweft.DSL and module attributes.



Attribute
Holds




@name
The domain name.


@variables
A map of name =&gt; %{type:, init:}. The state.


@actions
Primitives. params, bind, and body.


@methods
Compound tasks. params and alternatives.


@todo_list
The goal. A call, a goal, or a multigoal.



A body step is %{eval: %{…}} for a guard, or %{pointer_set: "/p", value: v} for an effect. A guard reads state with %{pointer_get: "/p"}.
A problem is a second module. It sets @source to the domain name, it overrides the @variables keys it cares about, and it carries its own @todo_list.

